    "intro_narrative": "You awaken in the belly of an enormous, brass-plated airship. The rhythmic hissing of steam and the clanking of heavy iron gears echo throughout the dimly lit chamber. This is the workshop of the infamous inventor, Professor Arkwright. He has locked the main navigation controls, leaving the ship on a collision course with the jagged peaks of the Iron Mountains. To regain control and transmit the emergency override signal, you must navigate a web of interconnected steampunk machinery. Scattered around the room are various gauges, dials, locks, and steam-powered engines. You need to figure out how these devices interact, tracing the flow of data and pressure from one mechanism to the next. The brass transmitter is your ultimate goal—it alone can send the signal to halt the engines. Keep a close eye on which device feeds into another; only by activating them in the correct sequence can you restore power to the ship's core and escape a fiery demise. Time is ticking, and the steam pressure is rising!",
    "narrative_style": "steampunk"
  },
